\section{Immunity}{

Susceptible people sit on a ladder of immunity strata, from stratum 1 (no
immunity) to stratum \code{n_imm = length(strata)}. Stratum parameters
(\code{rel_susceptibility}, \code{rel_transmissibility}, \code{rel_hosp}, \code{rel_death},
\code{waning_rate}, \code{initial_strata}) can be a single value, a vector by stratum
(length \code{n_imm}), or an \verb{n_age x n_imm} matrix. A vector whose length
matches both the number of age groups and of strata is taken to be by
stratum.
\itemize{
\item \code{rel_susceptibility}: multiplies \code{susceptibility}.
\item \code{rel_transmissibility}: multiplies the infectiousness of people infected
in that stratum.
\item \code{rel_hosp}: multiplies \code{p_hosp}. This is protection \emph{given infection};
total protection against hospitalisation is
\code{1 - rel_susceptibility * rel_hosp}.
\item \code{rel_death}: multiplies \code{p_death_hosp} and \code{p_death_comm}.
}

An infection keeps the stratum of the person infected, so these multipliers
apply throughout the infection. Everyone who recovers goes to a single
recovered compartment \code{R}, which is fully protected. People leave \code{R} at
rate \code{waning_rate_R} and enter the ladder at \code{R_to_stratum}. On the ladder,
people move from stratum k to k - 1 at rate \code{waning_rate[k]}.

Vaccination status is not tracked. Doses from \code{vacc_schedule} go to people
in strata below \code{vacc_stratum} and to people in \code{R}, in proportion. Doses to
\code{R} are counted but change nothing.

Initially a fraction \code{initial_R} of each group is in \code{R}. The rest are spread
over the strata by \code{initial_strata}. \code{I0} and \code{E0} are placed in stratum 1
and taken from its share.
}

